    not_duplicate_of: []  # 64aa
    pr_ref:  # 64aa
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family E). Consolidates F34.C1 + F34.C2 previously folded onto INV-murig. Full evidence remains on INV-murig's pass-34 discussion entry; this row provides discrete representation.\n\nThe audit's verdict: F34.C1 is STANDALONE because the same silent-confirm fall-through that INV-bitig's Phase 3 PR4 was meant to fix is alive on the boundary-axis-not-in-vocab case. Different mechanism than the empty-source-dir fall-through INV-bitig closed. Security-relevant.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`verify-claims` accepts an arbitrary boundary value in claim YAML (`constraint.boundary: <anything>`) without validating it against the io-boundaries vocabulary catalog. When the claim's boundary value is NOT in the vocabulary, `must_not_exist: true` returns verdict `confirmed` (silent false-positive).\n\n**F34.C1 evidence.** Authored an 8-claim YAML using intuitive boundary names: `network`, `process`, `database`, `filesystem`, plus a fictional `banana`. Actual io-boundaries CLI vocabulary (via `hypergumbo io-boundaries --json`):\n\n```\nenv_read, external_potential, fs_read, fs_write, ipc_recv,\nlogging, net_recv, net_send, subprocess\n```\n\n(9 categories.) Intersection with the intuitive names tested: 0. Result for each: `must_not_exist: true` → verdict `confirmed`. Codebase actively does network calls (per INV-dasig HF Hub access) and `subprocess.run` all over the place — yet `NO_NETWORK_CALLS` (boundary=`network`) and `NO_SHELL_CALLS` (boundary=`process`) both **silently confirm**.\n\n**F34.C2 cleaner repro.** `BOUNDARY_BANANA` (explicitly fictional value) silently confirms with details `\"No banana chains found.\"`. The boundary value is never validated against the io-boundaries vocabulary at YAML load time.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`verify_claims.py:236-267` does:\n```python\nentry = boundary_map.entries.get(claim.constraint_boundary)\nchain_count = len(entry.chains) if entry else 0\n```\n\nWhen `entry` is `None` (boundary value not in BoundaryMap), `chain_count = 0`. Then `must_not_exist` passes silently because the chain count is below the threshold. This is the SAME silent-confirm fall-through that INV-bitig was meant to fix; Phase 3 PR4's `ClaimVerdict.inconclusive` covered the empty-source-dir case but NOT the boundary-not-in-vocab case.\n\n## Invariant\n\nFor every `verify-claims` claim, `constraint.boundary` is validated against the canonical io-boundaries vocabulary at YAML load time. Unknown boundary values produce one of:\n\n1. **rc=2 at load** with `Error: unknown boundary value '<X>'; valid values: [...]` (preferred — stops processing on first invalid claim).\n2. **Verdict `inconclusive`** with reason `\"boundary value '<X>' not in vocabulary\"` (matches INV-bitig Phase 3 PR4's verdict shape for similar cases).\n\nPath (1) is stricter — catches typos before processing — and is more security-friendly. Path (2) preserves the verdict stream's continuity but requires the consumer to inspect `details`.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nAt `verify_claims.py:200-225` (`load_claims`), register a `boundary in BoundaryMap.entries.keys()` check after parsing each claim. Emit clear error on mismatch. Same registry-membership pattern as INV-murig describes for `config <unknown-language>` and `search --kind <invalid>` — extend the WI-bupim \"did-you-mean\" hint mechanism to cover this binding too.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F34.C1 + F34.C2** — INV-murig discussion entry 2026-06-02T17:13:XX (pass-34 batch; full mechanism enumeration in paragraphs labeled F34.C1 and F34.C2).\n\nLab notebook: pass 34 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-murig** (META: registry-membership validation gaps) — sibling under same parent.\n- Sibling: **INV-bitig** (closed — silent-confirm on empty source dir; sibling fall-through different mechanism).\n- Sibling: **WI-verify-claims-inconclusive-on-typo** (Family E — different verdict (inconclusive vs confirmed) but same load-time validation gap).\n- Sibling: **INV-fabov** (parent of INV-murig; silent input acceptance META).\n- Related security: **INV-dasig** (HF Hub access P0) — the boundary-NO_NETWORK_CALLS-confirms false-positive happens on a substrate that demonstrably violates the claim."  # 64aa
    fields: {}  # 64aa
